    "problem_statement": "# Filldown option with List values not working correctly\n\n## Description\n\nI found a bug in TextFSM when using the `Filldown` option with `List` values. The values are not being preserved correctly when a `Clear` action is triggered.\n\n## Steps to reproduce\n\nGiven the following template:\n```\nValue List,Filldown boo (on.)\nValue hoo (on.)\n\nStart\n  ^$boo -> Continue\n  ^$hoo -> Next.Record\n\nEOF\n```\n\nAnd the following input data:\n```\none\non0\non1\n```\n\n## Expected behavior\n\nThe `Filldown` option should preserve the list values across records, so the result should be:\n```\n[[['one'], 'one'], [['one', 'on0'], 'on0'], [['one', 'on0', 'on1'], 'on1']]\n```\n\n## Actual behavior\n\nThe values are being completely cleared instead of preserved when using the `Filldown` option with `List` values. This happens when a `Clear` action is triggered.\n\n## Additional information\n\nThis also affects more complex scenarios where nested capturing groups are used within List values. For example, when parsing structured data like:\n```\n Bob: 32 NC\n Alice: 27 NY\n Jeff: 45 CA\nJulia\n```\n\nThe values are not being preserved correctly when they should be.\n\nI believe the issue is in the `OnClearVar` method in the `TextFSMOptions` class, which is not handling the `Filldown` option correctly for List values.\n\n<END WRITING>"
